2. PERMITTED USES and RESTRICTIONS
       This License allows you to use each instance of  CacheGuard-OS  on  one
       and  only one logical machine (hardware or virtual machine). To benefit
       from optional paid services you consent to register your  appliance  to
       get a unique Serial Number (S/N). Depending on the optional features or
       embedded applications activated, a License Key may or may  not  be  re-
       quired.  You  expressly acknowledge that users and applications handled
       by CG-OS exist and are under your responsibility. WHERE A SERIAL NUMBER
       AND/OR  LICENSE  KEYS  HAVE  BEEN ISSUED, THEY CANNOT BE CHANGED ONCE A
       COPY OF CG-OS IS INSTALLED AND REGISTERED.

       By installing CG-OS on your own hardware or virtual  machine,  you  ac-
       knowledge that the machine is dedicated to running CG-OS for as long as
       CG-OS remains installed and operational on it. The combination of  your
       machine  and  CG-OS  constitutes an appliance (collectively, the APPLI-
       ANCE). If you decide to register the  APPLIANCE,  you  consent  to  the
       electronic  transmission to CACHEGUARD of certain technical information
       relating to the APPLIANCE, including, but not limited to, its  MAC  ad-
       dress,  licensed number of users, operating system version, and similar
       technical data. CACHEGUARD may collect  and  process  this  information
       solely for subscription management, and technical control purposes. You
       also consent to the APPLIANCE regularly transmitting its alive state to
       CACHEGUARD.  In  addition,  you  consent  to the APPLIANCE periodically
       checking for the availability  of  new  CG-OS  releases  by  contacting
       CACHEGUARD  online services. When the APPLIANCE is deployed on a public
       cloud in its PAYG (Pay As You Go) form, the registration  is  implicit;
       therefore,  you  consent  to  automatic registration and its underlying
       consequences. CACHEGUARD undertakes to process such data in  accordance
       with  applicable  data protection laws, including the General Data Pro-
       tection Regulation (GDPR), where applicable, and will not  use  it  for
       any other purpose.

