9. SSL mediation and Privacy
       The  SSL mediation feature integrated into CG-OS is designed to decrypt
       HTTPS traffic in order to cache and/or inspect its contents and  possi-
       bly block unwanted content. As HTTPS aims to give users privacy and se-
       curity, decrypting traffic in transit  (before  it  reaches  the  final
       client)  may violate ethical norms, employee privacy rights, and may be
       illegal in your jurisdiction. In jurisdictions where such  interception
       is  regulated  - including but not limited to those subject to the Gen-
       eral Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) -  the  organization  activating
       this  feature may be required to inform users in advance, obtain appro-
       priate consents, and implement adequate safeguards. By  activating  the
       SSL  mediation  feature,  you expressly acknowledge that you understand
       the technical and legal implications of doing so, that you  have  taken
       appropriate  legal advice where required, and that all resulting conse-
       quences are fully under your responsibility. CACHEGUARD shall  bear  no
       liability for any breach of applicable law arising from the use of this
       feature.


